{%- comment -%}
  HA — Cookie preferences link.

  Angela, 14 September 2026: a permanent "Cookie Preferences" link in the
  footer, so a visitor can change the choice they made on the banner.

  The banner itself is Shopify's own, switched on and region-gated under
  Settings > Customer privacy. Nothing here draws a banner or sets a cookie.
  This is one link that reopens Shopify's preferences dialog through the
  documented hook, `window.privacyBanner.showPreferences()`:
  https://shopify.dev/docs/api/customer-privacy

  It is an ordinary link first and a button second. The href is the privacy
  policy, so where the banner script has not loaded — a region the banner is
  not shown in, a browser with scripts off, the theme editor — the link still
  goes somewhere honest instead of doing nothing. When the hook is present the
  click is intercepted and the dialog opens in place.

  Rendered by ha-footer (the site) and ha-landing (the holding page, which has
  no footer of its own). The listener is bound once however many times the
  snippet renders.

  Accepts: label (string, defaults to "Cookie preferences").
{%- endcomment -%}

<a
  class="ha-cookie-prefs"
  href="{{ shop.privacy_policy.url | default: routes.root_url }}"
  data-ha-cookie-prefs
>{{ label | default: 'Cookie preferences' }}</a>

<script>
  (function () {
    if (window.haCookiePrefsBound) return;
    window.haCookiePrefsBound = true;
    document.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
      var link = event.target.closest('[data-ha-cookie-prefs]');
      if (!link) return;
      var banner = window.privacyBanner;
      if (banner && typeof banner.showPreferences === 'function') {
        event.preventDefault();
        banner.showPreferences();
      }
    });
  })();
</script>
